{"metadata":{"title":"MixpanelEncoding","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"MixpanelEncoding","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for your Mixpanel project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the project token, posts to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/track"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint of the project’s data residency"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose=1"},{"type":"text","text":", through a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and splits each batch to Mixpanel’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,000 events and 2 MB a request. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, waiting "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Mixpanel’s recommended"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s. The full jitter on top is Traffluent’s own choice. It drops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports any other status. The token goes in each event, so no header field is needed, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The project token is public: Mixpanel’s own apps and web pages ship it. The destination takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else. Never put the project’s secret or a service account’s credentials in an app; they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"belong to Mixpanel’s import API, for servers. The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty token, and for one with a character other than a letter or digit, which no project token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in the US, the EU or India, and Mixpanel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ingests nothing for it from another residency’s endpoint, so you pick the region on purpose.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own record identifier, with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Under Simplified ID Merge, Mixpanel shows a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session’s events under ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device:<session>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a sessionless record’s under its bare record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"$user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. Each event’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as is the endpoint’s, so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard context is sent as Mixpanel’s default properties (","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version_string","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_build_number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each record sent without a session. On a Mixpanel plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"starts with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ names do, one with a property Mixpanel reads for itself","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"text":"-prefixed one, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucket"},{"text":"), one of 255 properties or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"more counting the encoder’s own, one holding an array of 255 elements or more, one whose property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nests objects more than 3 deep, one whose event isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is before 1971 or has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch-milliseconds form, one tracked more than 119 hours before its batch is encoded or more than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an hour after, and one too large for Mixpanel. The destination reports each as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" whose reason is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel answers 200 even when it finds no valid event in a request. The endpoint asks for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"verbose=1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the answer’s body says so, ","type":"text"},{"code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drops the request and reports it as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with Mixpanel’s error as the reason. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"status","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of 1 means only that one event or more was well","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"formed: it doesn’t confirm that the token names a project, so a wrong region, or a token of no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored. Check the project’s Live View after setting the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination up.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel’s track API ingests only events from the last 5 days, and answers 200 to an older one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while storing nothing. So the destination drops and reports such a record rather than send it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The encoder leaves out a record tracked more than 119 hours (5 days less an hour, for clocks that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disagree) before its batch is encoded, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Each request has a deadline 119 hours after its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest record was tracked, and a request still being retried when it passes isn’t sent again: it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is reported as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Pass the factory’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"now:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clock of your own to test this.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog or Amplitude, use "},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MixpanelEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: mixpanel)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Mixpanel receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Mixpanel","title":"Sending to Mixpanel","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mixpanel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"projectToken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelRegion","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A6RegionO"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"now"},{"kind":"text","text":": () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Date","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelSetupError","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URLSessionTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSessionTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Mixpanel project of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"projectToken"},{"text":", whose data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resides in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"text":", with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession.shared"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"waits of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/mixpanel(projecttoken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)":{"title":"mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Mixpanel project of ","type":"text"},{"code":"projectToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resides in ","type":"text"},{"code":"region","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", through ","type":"text"},{"code":"transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/mixpanel(projecttoken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mixpanel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"projectToken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"region","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A6RegionO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transport","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"now","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Date","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelSetupError","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"topic"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder\/batchlimit","abstract":[{"text":"Mixpanel’s limits on one request: 2,000 events, 2,000,000 bytes of body, and 999,999 bytes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of one event.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","title":"batchLimit","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","title":"Choosing Destinations","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"link"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"BatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","title":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/track"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelSetupError":{"title":"MixpanelSetupError","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"couldn’t make a destination.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelsetuperror","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","type":"topic"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"title":"MixpanelEncodingError","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","type":"topic"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelRegion":{"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelregion","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The data residency of a Mixpanel project, which decides the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/track"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint its events are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"posted to."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","title":"MixpanelRegion","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError/timestampOutsideWindow":{"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror\/timestampoutsidewindow","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The record was tracked more than 119 hours before the batch was encoded or more than an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hour after it, or the clock the encoder reads gave a NaN or infinite time. Mixpanel’s track","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API drops an event more than 5 days old while answering 200, the hour to spare being for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queue on Mixpanel’s side and clocks that disagree, and rejects one more than an hour in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"future.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timestampOutsideWindow"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MixpanelEncodingError.timestampOutsideWindow","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/mixpanel":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mixpanel"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"mixpanel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel’s recommended schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s, with full jitter: a nominal wait of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2 seconds before the first retry, doubling up to 60 seconds. Mixpanel recommends the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule; the full jitter is Traffluent’s, as for every destination."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff\/mixpanel"}}}